  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Opera of Fuzhou sung in the Fuzhou dialect, formed in the late Qing and early Republic when the Rulin, Pingjiang and Jianghu troupe traditions merged; it is on China's national intangible heritage list (2006). Its music draws on the jianghu tunes, yangge, douqiang and folk xiaodiao, accompanied by bowed fiddles, flute and suona with a gong-and-drum section; the erhu card stands for its huqin fiddles and the generic bamboo-flute card for its flute.",
